-- Salesforce tool classification, after the Composio flip.
--
-- Salesforce moved from its own Connected App (whose consumer key no longer
-- resolves at any Salesforce login host) to Composio's managed OAuth app.
-- Its 60 curated tools plus the generated read_activity are new
-- NAMES, so the seven rows migration 082 wrote for the native sidecar's tool set
-- classify nothing that is served any more. Unclassified tools default
-- fail-secure — HITL on every write — which is safe and unusable, so this seeds
-- the real set.
--
-- Generated by connector-service scripts/classify-connector-tools.ts
-- --from-registry, every row decided from the registry's own categories (the
-- overlay's categoryOverrides) rather than the LLM relay, then reviewed by hand.
--
-- search_records (SOQL) carries NO sensitivity categories. It is read-only by
-- construction: SOQL has no DML, it reaches Salesforce's Query API, and the
-- vendor schema states the statement must start with SELECT. There is no
-- "sensitive read" dimension in this taxonomy — the five keys
-- (customerCommunication, financialActions, dataChanges, externalPublishing,
-- hiringDecisions) all describe effects a read does not have — so tagging one to
-- buy approval friction would be a false claim in the ledger.
--
-- Migration 082's native rows (read_record, delete_record, …) are deliberately
-- left in place: they name tools the COMPOSIO_DISABLED_CONNECTORS fallback still
-- serves, and a row for a tool nobody calls costs nothing.

-- Generated by scripts/classify-connector-tools.ts
-- Connector: salesforce (61 tools)
ON CONFLICT (tool_name, COALESCE(integration_type, ''), COALESCE(tenant_id, '__global__')) DO UPDATE
  SET categories = EXCLUDED.categories,
      tool_description_hash = EXCLUDED.tool_description_hash,
      reviewed_by = EXCLUDED.reviewed_by,
      classified_at = NOW();
